 "result_text": "`generate_uid()` now always returns a 64-character UID when you give it a prefix. A quick check of 2000 UIDs generated with the prefix `1.2.3.` gave a length of 64 every time. I didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `src/pydicom/uid.py`. It appended `secrets.randbelow(10 ** (64 - len(prefix)))` to the prefix. That number was sometimes shorter than the available digits, so the UID came out under 64 characters. This is what made the file meta information length vary and gave the intermittent `398 == 396` failure in `test_add_dataset`.\n\nThe random part now always has exactly `64 - len(prefix)` digits and never starts with zero.\n\nI didn't touch the `test_encoders.py::TestDatasetCompress::test_round_trip` flake, which the issue guessed was a memory re-use problem.",
